	(text "The Golden Rule for your Firmware\nBecause of the AD7193's /WEN bit, you must clear the bus before selecting a new chip. Your C/C++ function for reading these ADCs must follow this exact rigid sequence:\n\nAssert: Pull 595 Latch LOW.\n\nSelect: Send 11111110 (or whichever ADC you want).\n\nLock: Pull 595 Latch HIGH. (Target ADC is now active).\n\nCommunicate: Send your AD7193 command (starting with 0) and read your 24 bits of data.\n\nAssert: Pull 595 Latch LOW.\n\nClear: Send 11111111 (0xFF). (Active ADC ignores this because MSB is 1).\n\nLock: Pull 595 Latch HIGH. (All ADCs are now safely deselected)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.97 266.192 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d2e74017-7582-402d-9279-50c4faf4be96")
	)
